# Remote Agents — Local Development Secrets
#
# Copy this file to .dev.vars and fill in your values.
# .dev.vars is gitignored and never committed.
#
# Production: use `wrangler secret put <NAME>` for each variable.
# Local dev:  copy to .dev.vars and set values directly.
#
# All secrets flow: Cloudflare dashboard/wrangler → Worker env → container env vars.
# Nothing is baked into the Docker image or Dockerfile.

# ── LLM provider ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Anthropic API key.
# Used by the orchestrator to call Claude and injected into every container
# so `opencode serve` can make LLM API calls.
#
# Obtain: https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
# Format: sk-ant-...
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ── GitHub ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# GitHub personal access token (classic PAT or fine-grained PAT).
# Injected into containers so `gh` can authenticate, push branches,
# and open pull requests on your behalf.
#
# Classic PAT — required scopes: repo, workflow
# Fine-grained PAT — required permissions:
#   Contents: Read and write
#   Pull requests: Read and write
#   Workflows: Read and write  (only needed if agents modify workflow files)
#
# Obtain: https://github.com/settings/tokens
# Format: ghp_... (classic) or github_pat_... (fine-grained)
GH_TOKEN=

# ── Linear / lb ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Linear API key used by `lb` inside containers to sync issue state,
# update statuses, and create/read issues.
#
# Obtain: https://linear.app/settings/api  →  "Personal API keys"
# Format: lin_api_...
LINEAR_API_KEY=

# ── Git identity ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Name and email used for git commits made by remote agents.
# Injected as GIT_AUTHOR_NAME / GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL env vars; the container
# entrypoint runs `git config user.name` and `git config user.email`.
#
# These show up in git log as the commit author.
# Use something that identifies automated commits, e.g. a bot account.
GIT_AUTHOR_NAME=Remote Agent
GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=agent@example.com
